  "term": "Cylert",
  "definition": "Cylert is a central nervous system stimulant drug in the oxazolidine group, also known as pemoline. It has effects similar to other stimulants, though its exact action is unclear, and it was withdrawn from the U.S. market because it was linked to life-threatening liver failure.",
